# ==============================================================
# Netlify _redirects
#
# This repo deploys from GitHub, so every tracked file is served
# at its path - including the internal docs. These rules hide the
# ones that are for us, not for customers.
#
# The trailing "!" forces the rule. Without it Netlify serves an
# existing file in preference to a redirect, and these files DO
# exist in the deploy - so the force is the whole point.
#
# The files stay in the repo (version-controlled, useful); they
# are just not reachable from the web.
# ==============================================================

